*.pyc
*.vcd
*.vpd
.Xil/
.venv/
__pycache__/
ASIC/*/logs
ASIC/*/outputs
ASIC/*/reports
ASIC/*/work
ASIC/*/calibre_runs
ASIC/romlibs
build/
build_soc/
csrc/
results.xml
results_*.xml
sim_build/
simv
simv.daidir/
ucli.key
vc_hdrs.h
verif/*/*.log
verif/*/csrc/
verif/*/simv_*
verif/*/simv_*.daidir/
verif/*/ucli.key
verif/cdc/build/
verif/elab_strict/build/
vivado*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str
# Synopsys DC analysis DB + HAPS FPGA-prototype build outputs (not source)
/AN.DB/
# Ignore the BUILD OUTPUTS ONLY. These rules used to be /fpga/haps-sx/ and
# /fpga/haps-sx-pc/, which also swallowed ~230 KB of hand-written source --
# the board top, the .cob, the constraints and the build scripts -- despite
# the comment above saying "not source". Git cannot re-include a path under
# an excluded directory, so a negation would not have worked; the rules have
# to name the build dirs directly.
/fpga/haps-sx/build/
/fpga/haps-sx-pc/build/
# Tool droppings written into $PWD rather than work/. Genus, Innovus and IC
# Validator all log relative to the directory they were LAUNCHED from, so a
# one-off probe (`genus -batch -command get_db`, `icv`, or an ad-hoc
# `innovus -files experiment.tcl`) lands them wherever it was started, which
# the ASIC/*/{logs,work} rules do not reach.
#
# These rules are deliberately NOT anchored with a leading slash. They started
# out as /genus.log* etc., which only ever matched the repo root -- and then a
# scratch run in ASIC/genus-innovus/holdexp/ dropped 700 KB of innovus.log*,
# innovus.logv* and innovus.cmd* into a directory that also holds hand-written
# .tcl, so neither the anchored rules nor a whole-directory ignore would do.
# Unanchored, they follow the tool to whatever directory it was invoked in.
#
# `log*` covers three families in one glob and is meant to: the plain log, the
# VERBOSE log Innovus writes alongside it (innovus.logv -- this is a distinct
# file, not a typo for .log), and the rotation suffixes both take on re-runs
# (innovus.log1, innovus.logv2, innovus.cmd2, genus.log1, ...).
genus.log*
genus.cmd*
innovus.log*
innovus.cmd*
# Anchored, unlike the above: a stray stderr capture at the root is a dropping,
# but "err.txt" is an ordinary name for a test fixture somewhere in verif/.
/err.txt
.icv.*
# Baseline P&R snapshots. scripts/ci/asic_stage_report.sh takes BASELINE_DIR and
# diffs the current run against one of these; each is a full copy of
# logs/ outputs/ reports/ work/ and runs to ~2.7 GB. The existing
# ASIC/*/{logs,outputs,reports,work} rules sit one directory level too high to
# match them, since the copy nests them under ASIC/*/baseline_<date>/.
ASIC/*/baseline_*/

# MkDocs build output
site/

# Per-iteration ASIC run directories. Each is 2-3GB and self-describing
# (config/ holds a copy of every script and constraint used). Reproducible
# from the git SHA recorded in its MANIFEST.txt, so not tracked.
ASIC/genus-innovus/runs/
ASIC/genus-innovus/baseline_*/

# ── Tool sandboxes and work libraries (2026-08-09) ──────────────────────────
# ~370 MB of untracked droppings accumulated in one week. The globs are
# deliberately loose: every one of these directories was an ad-hoc sandbox
# invented mid-investigation, so anchoring to today's exact names just means
# the same bulk reappears next week under a new one.

# Xcelium/HAL work library, written to the repo root by verif/lint/full/hal_lint.sh.
/xcelium.d/

# HAL emits these beside wherever it was launched; regenerated every run.
hal.design_facts
hal.log
hal.rpt

# Conformal LEC sandboxes. run_lec.sh is pointed at these via its *_DIR knobs,
# so each is a full copy of scripts/ + inputs/ plus netlists, work/fv scratch
# and reports. NOTE: these also shadow the real flow scripts — never edit a
# script inside one, the edit is silently lost (see docs/tapeout notes).
ASIC/*/lec_*shadow/

# Ad-hoc Innovus probe scratch. ASIC/*/work matches only the literal `work`,
# so work_pgprobe/, work_probe/ and the next work_<something> escape it.
ASIC/*/work_*/

# Innovus console capture from the hold experiments. The .tcl beside them is
# the reproducible input and IS tracked; the .out is just stdout.
ASIC/*/holdexp/*.out

# Cocotb generates the per-node DUT filelists from the Makefile.
cocotb/*/dut_src_*.f

# Claude Code session automation (agent definitions, workflow scripts).
# Local tooling, not design data -- and .claude/settings.local.json can carry
# machine-specific paths. Track deliberately if a workflow becomes shared.
.claude/

# v2lvs netlist-translation log. Written wherever the LVS flow is invoked
# from, so it is matched anywhere rather than at a fixed path -- one run of
# it reached 86 MB. The flow that produces it (ASIC/lvs-flow) IS tracked.
v2lvs.log

# Session scratch space. Never design data.
scratchpad/
